# explorer2-api's command (zega-cloud/explorer2-api/fly.toml entrypoint) in Docker at shared-cpu-1x limits; curl from the host
## preflight from https://explorer2.zega.dev, no token
HTTP/1.1 204 No Content
access-control-allow-methods: GET, POST, DELETE
access-control-allow-headers: authorization, content-type
access-control-max-age: 7200
vary: Origin
access-control-allow-origin: https://explorer2.zega.dev
allow: POST

## preflight from https://evil.example
HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden
vary: Origin
allow: POST
content-length: 0

## GET /graph from explorer2, no token
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
content-type: application/json
vary: Origin
access-control-allow-origin: https://explorer2.zega.dev
content-length: 35

{"error":"unauthorized","ok":false}

## GET /graph from http://localhost:8788 with the token
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
content-type: application/json
vary: Origin
access-control-allow-origin: http://localhost:8788
content-length: 43

{"ok":true,"result":{"nodes":[],"rels":[]}}

## GET /graph from https://evil.example with the token (answered, but no allow-origin, so a browser blocks it)
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
content-type: application/json
vary: Origin
content-length: 43

{"ok":true,"result":{"nodes":[],"rels":[]}}

